# environments
# `.venv/` and the cache directories are anchored to the repo root so that a directory
# of the same name nested inside src/ or tests/ can never be silently excluded.
# `__pycache__/` is deliberately LEFT unanchored: it exists at every depth
# (src/etl/__pycache__, tests/__pycache__, ...) and must be ignored at all of them.
# `tests/test_repo_hygiene.py` enforces the first rule and exempts the second.
/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/

# Data and models (large or regenerable)
#
# These are anchored with a leading "/" on purpose. An unanchored "models/" matches a
# directory named "models" at ANY depth, which silently excluded `src/models/` — the
# classifier training module — from the repository. A clean clone could not import it,
# so `make check` and `make smoke` both failed. Found by the T10.2 clean-clone check.
/data/raw/
/data/raw_smoke/
/data/external/
/data/processed/
/data/processed_smoke/
/data/warehouse/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/models/
/models_smoke/
*.joblib

# Logs and smoke outputs
/logs/
/logs_smoke/
/reports_smoke/
/config/frozen_config.smoke.yaml
/reports/daily/

# local secrets
.env
